  "headline": "The derived ceiling was NEVER violated, so doc 47 SS3 survives its falsification test. But measured accuracy falls further BELOW the ceiling as demand grows, so beyond m=1 the binding limit is OPTIMISATION, not representation -- which is exactly the separation SS4's instrument was built to make.",
  "M3_at_floor": "At m=3 BOTH arms sit at the S-shuffle floor (0.4807/0.4780 vs floor 0.5007), so M3 cells FAIL the floor precondition and are reported as FAILED, not as 'below ceiling'.",
  "spectrum_relieves": "Cell-dependent and registered as such: S2 lifts M2w from 0.6720 to 0.8507 but LOWERS M2 (0.6827 -> 0.6467). Widening the spectrum raises what is representable; whether it is TRAINABLE depends on band spacing. doc 47 SS15 warned that minimum-K is a representational statement, not a recipe -- this measures that.",
